Title: Secured & Monitored Web Infrastructure (TLS + Firewalls + Monitoring)

ASCII diagram:
[User] -> [DNS] -> [LB (TLS)] -> [Web+App #1] -> [MySQL Primary]
                         |              \-> [Monitoring Agent]
                         -> [Web+App #2] -> [MySQL Primary]
                                        \-> [Monitoring Agent]
[Firewall #1: Internet->LB 80/443]
[Firewall #2: LB->Web/App internal HTTP/health]
[Firewall #3: Web/App->DB 3306 only]
[Monitoring backend (Sumo/Datadog/ELK/CloudWatch)] <- agents

Added & why:
- 3 Firewalls: least privilege, reduced attack surface
- SSL certificate: HTTPS (encryption, integrity, server auth)
- Monitoring agents: collect CPU, RAM, QPS, latency, 5xx, logs

What are firewalls for? Filter traffic by IP/port/protocol
Why HTTPS? Confidentiality, integrity, authentication
What is monitoring for? Visibility, alerting, capacity planning, troubleshooting
How is data collected? Agents push/scrape metrics/logs at intervals
Monitor web QPS? Enable Nginx stub_status or app metrics; dashboard + alert

Issues to highlight:
- TLS only at LB: backend LB->Web/App plaintext unless internal TLS
- Single writable MySQL: write SPOF; need failover/promotion
- Same components on each host: larger blast radius; resource contention
